// @description Indicates info about a certain user.
// @param access_hash Access hash of the user, see here » for more info. If this flag is set, when updating the local peer database , generate a virtual flag called min_access_hash , which is: - Set to true if min is set AND -- The phone flag is not set OR -- The phone flag is set and the associated phone number string is non-empty - Set to false otherwise. Then, apply both access_hash and min_access_hash to the local database if: - min_access_hash is false OR - min_access_hash is true AND -- There is no locally cached object for this user OR -- There is no access_hash in the local cache OR -- The cached object's min_access_hash is also true If the final merged object stored to the database has the min_access_hash field set to true, the related access_hash is only suitable to use in inputPeerPhotoFileLocation » , to directly download the profile pictures of users, everywhere else a inputPeer*FromMessage constructor will have to be generated as specified here » . Bots can also use min access hashes in some conditions, by passing 0 instead of the min access hash.
// @param apply_min_photo If set and min is set, the value of photo can be used to update the local database, see the documentation of that flag for more info.
// @param attach_menu_enabled Whether we installed the attachment menu web app offered by this bot. When updating the local peer database , do not apply changes to this field if the min flag is set.
// @param bot Is this user a bot? Changes to this flag should invalidate the local userFull cache for this user ID, see here » for more info.
// @param bot_active_users Monthly Active Users (MAU) of this bot (may be absent for small bots).
// @param bot_attach_menu Whether this bot offers an attachment menu web app
// @param bot_business Whether this bot can be connected to a user as specified here » .
// @param bot_can_edit Whether we can edit the profile picture, name, about text and description of this bot because we own it. When updating the local peer database , do not apply changes to this field if the min flag is set. Changes to this flag (if min is not set) should invalidate the local userFull cache for this user ID.
// @param bot_can_manage_bots If set, this bot is a manager bot that can create and manage managed bots » on behalf of the user.
// @param bot_chat_history Can the bot see all messages in groups?
// @param bot_forum_can_manage_topics If set, this bot supports bot forum topics » , and users (not just the bot!) are allowed to create and manage bot forum topics in their private chat with the bot.
// @param bot_forum_view If set, this bot supports bot forum topics » .
// @param bot_guestchat If set, this bot can be invoked as a guest in chats » .
// @param bot_has_main_app If set, this bot has configured a Main Mini App » .
// @param bot_info_version Version of the bot_info field in userFull , incremented every time it changes. Changes to this flag should invalidate the local userFull cache for this user ID, see here » for more info.
// @param bot_inline_geo Whether the bot can request our geolocation in inline mode
// @param bot_inline_placeholder Inline placeholder for this inline bot
// @param bot_nochats Can the bot be added to groups?
// @param bot_verification_icon Describes a bot verification icon » .
// @param close_friend Whether we marked this user as a close friend, see here » for more info . When updating the local peer database , do not apply changes to this field if the min flag is set.
// @param color The user's accent color .
// @param contact Whether this user is a contact When updating the local peer database , do not apply changes to this field if the min flag is set.
// @param contact_require_premium See here for more info on this flag » .
// @param deleted Whether the account of this user was deleted. Changes to this flag should invalidate the local userFull cache for this user ID, see here » for more info.
// @param emoji_status Emoji status
// @param fake If set, this user was reported by many users as a fake or scam user: be careful when interacting with them.
// @param first_name First name. When updating the local peer database , apply changes to this field only if: - The min flag is not set OR - The min flag is set AND -- The min flag of the locally cached user entry is set.
// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param flags2 Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param id ID of the user, see here » for more info and the available ID range.
// @param lang_code Language code of the user
// @param last_name Last name. When updating the local peer database , apply changes to this field only if: - The min flag is not set OR - The min flag is set AND -- The min flag of the locally cached user entry is set.
// @param min See min
// @param mutual_contact Whether this user is a mutual contact. When updating the local peer database , do not apply changes to this field if the min flag is set.
// @param phone Phone number. When updating the local peer database , apply changes to this field only if: - The min flag is not set OR - The min flag is set AND -- The min flag of the locally cached user entry is set.
// @param photo Profile picture of user. When updating the local peer database , apply changes to this field only if: - The min flag is not set OR - The min flag is set AND -- The apply_min_photo flag is set OR -- The min flag of the locally cached user entry is set.
// @param premium Whether this user is a Telegram Premium user Changes to this flag should invalidate the local userFull cache for this user ID, see here » for more info. Changes to this flag if the self flag is set should also trigger the following calls, to refresh the respective caches: - The help.getConfig cache - The messages.getTopReactions cache if the bot flag is not set
// @param profile_color The user's profile color .
// @param restricted Access to this user must be restricted for the reason specified in restriction_reason
// @param restriction_reason Contains the reason why access to this user must be restricted.
// @param scam This may be a scam user
// @param self Whether this user indicates the currently logged in user
// @param send_paid_messages_stars If set, the user has enabled paid messages » , we might need to pay the specified amount of Stars to send them messages, depending on the configured exceptions: check userFull . send_paid_messages_stars or users.getRequirementsToContact to see if the currently logged in user actually has to pay or not, see here » for the full flow.
// @param status Online status of user. When updating the local peer database , apply changes to this field only if: - The min flag is not set OR - The min flag is set AND -- The min flag of the locally cached user entry is set OR -- The locally cached user entry is equal to userStatusEmpty .
// @param stories_hidden Whether we have hidden » all active stories of this user. When updating the local peer database , do not apply changes to this field if the min flag is set.
// @param stories_max_id Summary of the user's active stories » . When updating the local peer database , do not apply changes to this field if the min flag of the incoming constructor is set.
// @param stories_unavailable No stories from this user are visible.
// @param support Whether this is an official support user
// @param username Main active username. When updating the local peer database , apply changes to this field only if: - The min flag is not set OR - The min flag is set AND -- The min flag of the locally cached user entry is set. Changes to this flag should invalidate the local userFull cache for this user ID if the above conditions are respected and the bot_can_edit flag is also set.
// @param usernames Additional usernames. When updating the local peer database , apply changes to this field only if: - The min flag is not set OR - The min flag is set AND -- The min flag of the locally cached user entry is set. Changes to this flag (if the above conditions are respected) should invalidate the local userFull cache for this user ID.
// @param verified Whether this user is verified
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/bots/attach
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/bots/connected-business-bots
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/bots/guest-mode
