// @description List of actions that are possible when interacting with this user, to be shown as suggested actions in the chat action bar » , see here » for more info.
// @param add_contact Whether we can add the user as contact
// @param autoarchived Whether this peer was automatically archived according to privacy settings and can be unarchived
// @param block_contact Whether we can block the user
// @param business_bot_can_reply This flag is set if both business_bot_id and business_bot_manage_url are set and connected business bots » can reply to messages in this chat, as specified by the settings during initial configuration .
// @param business_bot_id Contains the ID of the business bot » managing this chat, used to display info about the bot in the action bar.
// @param business_bot_manage_url Contains a deep link » , used to open a management menu in the business bot. This flag is set if and only if business_bot_id is set.
// @param business_bot_paused This flag is set if both business_bot_id and business_bot_manage_url are set and all connected business bots » were paused in this chat using account.toggleConnectedBotPaused » .
// @param charge_paid_message_stars All users that must pay us » to send us private messages will have this flag set only for us , containing the amount of required stars, see here » for more info on paid messages.
// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param geo_distance Distance in meters between us and this peer
// @param invite_members If set, this is a recently created group chat to which new members can be invited
// @param name_change_date When was the user's name last changed.
// @param need_contacts_exception Whether a special exception for contacts is needed
// @param phone_country The country code of the user's phone number.
// @param photo_change_date When was the user's photo last changed.
// @param registration_month Used to display the user's registration year and month, the string is in MM.YYYY format, where MM is the registration month ( 1-12 ), and YYYY is the registration year.
// @param report_geo Whether we can report a geogroup as irrelevant for this location
// @param report_spam Whether we can still report the user for spam
// @param request_chat_broadcast This flag is set if request_chat_title and request_chat_date fields are set and the join request » is related to a channel (otherwise if only the request fields are set, the join request » is related to a chat).
// @param request_chat_date If set, this is a private chat with an administrator of a chat or channel to which the user sent a join request, and this field contains the timestamp when the join request » was sent.
// @param request_chat_title If set, this is a private chat with an administrator of a chat or channel to which the user sent a join request, and this field contains the chat/channel's title.
// @param share_contact Whether we can share the user's contact
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/action-bar
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/bots/connected-business-bots
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/invites#join-requests
