// @description Hide sent reply keyboard
// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param selective Use this flag if you want to remove the keyboard for specific users only. Targets: 1) users that are @mentioned in the text of the Message object; 2) if the bot's message is a reply (has reply_to_message_id), sender of the original message. Example: A user votes in a poll, bot returns confirmation message in reply to the vote and removes the keyboard for that user, while still showing the keyboard with poll options to users who haven't voted yet
// @see https://core.telegram.org/constructor/true
// @see https://core.telegram.org/mtproto/TL-combinators#conditional-fields
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/%23
replyKeyboardHide#a03e5b85 flags:# selective:flags.2?true = ReplyMarkup;
// @description Force the user to send a reply
// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param placeholder The placeholder to be shown in the input field when the keyboard is active; 1-64 characters.
// @param selective Use this parameter if you want to show the keyboard to specific users only. Targets: 1) users that are @mentioned in the text of the Message object; 2) if the bot's message is a reply (has reply_to_message_id), sender of the original message. Example: A user requests to change the bot's language, bot replies to the request with a keyboard to select the new language. Other users in the group don't see the keyboard.
// @param single_use Requests clients to hide the keyboard as soon as it's been used. The keyboard will still be available, but clients will automatically display the usual letter-keyboard in the chat – the user can press a special button in the input field to see the custom keyboard again.
// @see https://core.telegram.org/constructor/true
// @see https://core.telegram.org/mtproto/TL-combinators#conditional-fields
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/%23
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/string
replyKeyboardForceReply#86b40b08 flags:# single_use:flags.1?true selective:flags.2?true placeholder:flags.3?string = ReplyMarkup;
// @description Represents a reply keyboard
// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param persistent Requests clients to always show the keyboard when the regular keyboard is hidden.
// @param placeholder The placeholder to be shown in the input field when the keyboard is active; 1-64 characters.
// @param resize Requests clients to resize the keyboard vertically for optimal fit (e.g., make the keyboard smaller if there are just two rows of buttons). If not set, the custom keyboard is always of the same height as the app's standard keyboard.
// @param rows Button row
// @param selective Use this parameter if you want to show the keyboard to specific users only. Targets: 1) users that are @mentioned in the text of the Message object; 2) if the bot's message is a reply (has reply_to_message_id), sender of the original message. Example: A user requests to change the bot's language, bot replies to the request with a keyboard to select the new language. Other users in the group don't see the keyboard.
// @param single_use Requests clients to hide the keyboard as soon as it's been used. The keyboard will still be available, but clients will automatically display the usual letter-keyboard in the chat – the user can press a special button in the input field to see the custom keyboard again.
// @see https://core.telegram.org/constructor/true
// @see https://core.telegram.org/mtproto/TL-combinators#conditional-fields
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/%23
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/KeyboardButtonRow
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/Vector%20t
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/string
replyKeyboardMarkup#85dd99d1 flags:# resize:flags.0?true single_use:flags.1?true selective:flags.2?true persistent:flags.4?true rows:Vector<KeyboardButtonRow> placeholder:flags.3?string = ReplyMarkup;
