// @description Details about the authorization request, for more info click here »
// @param bot Username of a bot, which will be used for user authorization. If not specified, the current bot's username will be assumed. The url's domain must be the same as the domain linked with the bot. See Linking your domain to the bot for more details.
// @param browser The browser the user used to make the OAuth request
// @param domain The domain name of the website on which the user will log in.
// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param ip The IP address of the user making the OAuth request
// @param is_app Set if an OAuth request originated from an app rather than a website; when set, domain must be replaced in the confirmation prompt by verified_app_name (if present) or "Unverified App"
// @param match_codes A list of emojis or codes, one of which is currently being shown on the login page of the website/app; the user must select the matching one and pass it to messages.acceptUrlAuth . match_code
// @param match_codes_first Can only be set if match_codes is also set; if set, clients must ask the user to select the matching code before showing the rest of the login confirmation UI, and must validate the selection with messages.checkUrlAuthMatchCode before proceeding
// @param platform The platform (operating system) of the user that made the OAuth request
// @param region The location of the user, inferred from the IP address
// @param request_phone_number The app/website is requesting the user's phone number; if the user consents, set share_phone_number when calling messages.acceptUrlAuth
// @param request_write_access Whether the bot would like to send messages to the user
// @param user_id_hint May contain the ID of the account for which the login request was created; if it matches a logged-in account, clients should automatically switch to that account and re-invoke messages.requestUrlAuth before showing the prompt
// @param verified_app_name Can only be set if is_app is set and the app is verified; must replace domain in the confirmation prompt when present
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/url-authorization
// @see https://core.telegram.org/constructor/true
// @see https://core.telegram.org/method/messages.acceptUrlAuth
// @see https://core.telegram.org/method/messages.checkUrlAuthMatchCode
// @see https://core.telegram.org/method/messages.requestUrlAuth
// @see https://core.telegram.org/mtproto/TL-combinators#conditional-fields
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/%23
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/User
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/Vector%20t
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/long
// @see https://core.telegram.org/type/string
// @see https://core.telegram.org/widgets/login#linking-your-domain-to-the-bot
urlAuthResultRequest#f8f8eb1e flags:# request_write_access:flags.0?true request_phone_number:flags.1?true match_codes_first:flags.5?true bot:User domain:string browser:flags.2?string platform:flags.2?string ip:flags.2?string region:flags.2?string match_codes:flags.3?Vector<string> user_id_hint:flags.4?long = UrlAuthResult;
// @description Details about an accepted authorization request, for more info click here »
