// @description Describes a group call .
// @param access_hash Group call access hash
// @param can_change_join_muted Whether the current user can change the value of the join_muted flag using phone.toggleGroupCallSettings . Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param can_change_messages_enabled Whether the current user may enable or disable the in-call message overlay » . Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param can_start_video Whether you can start streaming video into the call. Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param conference Whether this is an E2E conference call.
// @param creator Whether the current user created this group call. Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param default_send_as Default peer displayed as the author of live story comments and reactions » . Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param id Group call ID
// @param invite_link Invitation link for a conference call » . Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param join_date_asc Specifies the ordering to use when locally sorting by date and displaying in the UI group call participants. Set only when the call is created and never changed afterwards, so it is not applied from a min constructor.
// @param join_muted Whether the user should be muted upon joining the call. Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param listeners_hidden Whether the listeners list is hidden and cannot be fetched using phone.getGroupParticipants . The phone.groupParticipants.count and groupCall.participants_count counters will still include listeners.
// @param messages_enabled Whether the in-call message overlay » is enabled
// @param min Whether this is a partial constructor that must be merged into a previously cached non- min constructor, following the rules described above.
// @param participants_count Participant count
// @param record_start_date When was the recording started
// @param record_video_active Whether the group call is currently being recorded
// @param rtmp_stream Whether this call uses RTMP livestream mode »
// @param schedule_date When is the call scheduled to start
// @param schedule_start_subscribed Whether we subscribed to the scheduled call. Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param send_paid_messages_stars Minimum Stars donation required from users other than the live story owner to send a paid comment » ; 0 or no value allows free comments
// @param stream_dc_id Media DC ID to use for RTMP stream requests » . Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param title Group call title
// @param unmuted_video_count Number of people currently streaming video into the call. Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param unmuted_video_limit Maximum number of people allowed to stream video into the call. Must be ignored if the min flag is set.
// @param version Revision used to apply group call updates »
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/group-calls
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/group-calls#applying-group-call-updates
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/group-calls#conference-calls
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/group-calls#downloading-media-chunks
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/group-calls#in-call-messages
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/group-calls#paid-live-story-comments
