// @param flags Flags, see TL conditional fields
// @param from_id ID of the peer that created the topic
// @param hidden Whether the topic is hidden (only valid for the "General" topic, id=1 )
// @param icon_color If no custom emoji icon is specified, specifies the color of the fallback topic icon (RGB), one of 0x6FB9F0 , 0xFFD67E , 0xCB86DB , 0x8EEE98 , 0xFF93B2 , or 0xFB6F5F .
// @param icon_emoji_id ID of the custom emoji used as topic icon.
// @param id Topic ID
// @param my Whether the topic was created by the current user
// @param notify_settings Notification settings
// @param peer Contains the supergroup/private chat where the topic is located. This field is useful especially when this object is returned by methods like messages.getMessages , which can return messages and forum topics belonging to different (private chat) peers in the same method call, making it impossible to tell the topic's peer based on the method call parameters or surrounding context.
// @param pinned Whether the topic is pinned
// @param read_inbox_max_id Position up to which all incoming messages are read.
// @param read_outbox_max_id Position up to which all outgoing messages are read.
// @param short Whether this constructor is a reduced version of the full topic information. If set, only the my , closed , id , date , title , icon_color , icon_emoji_id and from_id parameters will contain valid information. Reduced info is usually only returned in topic-related admin log events » and in the messages.channelMessages constructor: if needed, full information can be fetched using messages.getForumTopicsByID .
// @param title Topic title
// @param title_missing If set, the topic has no user-defined title, can only be set for the per-user topics of bot forums ; if this field is set, the topic title likely needs to be changed by the bot.
// @param top_message ID of the last message that was sent to this topic
// @param unread_count Number of unread messages
// @param unread_mentions_count Number of unread mentions
// @param unread_poll_votes_count Number of unread votes cast in non-anonymous polls » owned by the user in this forum topic.
// @param unread_reactions_count Number of unread reactions to messages you sent
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/custom-emoji
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/drafts
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/forum#bot-forums
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/forum#forum-topics
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/mentions
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/poll#unread-poll-votes
// @see https://core.telegram.org/api/recent-actions
// @see https://core.telegram.org/constructor/messages.channelMessages
